Expose the server's key to the mobile bindings

Sending an IPv6 packet through the mobile wrapper goes to ipv6rwc, which has to
find the destination's ed25519 key before it can write: it buffers a single
packet while that lookup runs and forgets the answer after two minutes of
silence. The tunnel talks to exactly one server, so it is cheaper to learn that
key once and address the node directly.

  Core.ProbeNode          nodeinfo request by key; rides the protocol layer, so
                          it answers without an established session
  ReadWriteCloser.KeyForAddress  the key ipv6rwc already learned for an address
  mobile.SendToKey / KeyForAddress / ProbeNode   the three of them, bound for Kotlin

